{
  "rules_version": "1",
  "engine": "1",
  "note": "Prompt-cleaning catalogue, shared by both SDKs (bundled byte-identical) and copied to the ID Side cloud. Every pattern is written in a portable subset that Python's re and JavaScript's RegExp read alike; scripts and tests in both SDKs hold it. A pattern's value is its capture group `group`; a match in which that group took no part is context that rules a value out (four numbers after a version word), and the engine skips it whole. The id of a detector is what an organization's policy names and what counts are reported under: ids are added, never renamed.",
  "normalization": {
    "note": "Each code point of a text is mapped on its own: dropped if it is in `ignorable`, otherwise decomposed (NFKD), stripped of the code points in `combining`, with each code point listed in `equivalents` written as its ASCII equivalent; a code point above U+FFFF is written U+FFFD. Detectors read that shadow; custom terms, domains and keywords read it with A-Z lowered to a-z.",
